1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY & PROBLEM STATEMENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modern engineering teams deploy microservices, staging clusters, and cloud 
storage faster than internal security operations can catalog them. This speed 
creates "Shadow IT": forgotten staging subdomains (staging-auth.corp.com), 
unauthenticated API documentation portals (/swagger-ui, /graphiql), and public 
web server roots inadvertently exposing configuration dotfiles (.env), database 
backups (.sql), or git repositories (.git) to search engine web crawlers.

Security analysts and penetration testers use Google Dorking (advanced search 
operators such as site:, filetype:, inurl:) to discover these exposed assets. 
However, manual reconnaissance fails due to three fundamental bottlenecks:

1. Aggressive Anti-Bot Barriers:
   Google deploys strict automated defense systems that issue CAPTCHAs and IP 
   rate-limits after 3 to 5 rapid automated queries.
2. Fragmented & Unstructured Output:
   Traditional CLI tools dump disconnected terminal text or raw CSV dumps that 
   lack hierarchical relationships and asset context.
3. Absence of Actionable Remediation:
   Flagging a vulnerability without providing the exact web server directive, 
   cloud policy, or credential rotation steps leaves engineering teams exposed.

ReconFlow AI converts SerpApi into an autonomous, defensive External Attack 
Surface Management (EASM) agent. Given an enterprise target domain, ReconFlow:
• Bypasses bot barriers via SerpApi proxy infrastructure.
• Executes an intelligent multi-pass sweep across internal hosts (Phase 1) and 
  third-party shadow ecosystems (Phase 2).
• Normalizes FQDNs and prunes false positives.
• Tiers risks under OWASP testing standards (CRITICAL -> INFO).
• Renders findings onto an interactive React Flow canvas with automated, 
  copy-paste defensive remediation playbooks.


